</head>

<body lang=EN-US style='tab-interval:.5in'>

<div class=WordSection1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Comprehensive
Project Documentation: Hybrid <span class=SpellE>Blockchain</span> <span
class=SpellE>Jewellery</span> Tracking System</span><span style='font-size:
24.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;
mso-border-bottom-alt:solid #CCCCCC .75pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in'>

<h2><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1. Preliminary Investigation<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1.1 Problem Identification<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
The luxury <span class=SpellE>jewellery</span> market, valued at hundreds of
billions globally, is plagued by two significant issues: counterfeiting and the
untraceable movement of stolen goods. Secondary market retailers and
independent buyers often struggle to verify the true authenticity and origin of
high-value items like diamond rings and gold necklaces. Traditional paper-based
grading certificates (such as GIA certificates) are susceptible to loss,
degradation, or outright forgery. Consequently, this leads to a massive
breakdown in consumer trust and millions of dollars in financial losses
annually.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1.2 Problem Statement / Definition<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
There is a critical demand for a secure, tamper-proof, and decentralized
tracking system capable of logging the entire lifecycle of a premium <span
class=SpellE>jewellery</span> asset. The proposed &quot;<span class=SpellE>Luxe</span>
<span class=SpellE>Blockchain</span>&quot; system must provide immutable proof
of authenticity from the moment of manufacture, secure ownership transfer
capabilities, and a hybrid architecture. This hybrid approach balances the
unparalleled transparency of a <span class=SpellE>blockchain</span> with the
privacy, scalability, and speed of a traditional database system.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1.3 Purpose, Objectives, and Goals<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
- <b>Immutable Provenance:</b> To record the initial minting of <span
class=SpellE>jewellery</span> on a decentralized ledger to guarantee
authenticity that cannot be retrospectively altered.<br>
- <b>Ownership Tracking:</b> To facilitate, record, and verify the transfer of
ownership between manufacturers, retailers (shops), and end-users seamlessly.<br>
- <b>Hybrid Architecture Integration:</b> To securely store sensitive metadata
(such as high-res images, personal user details, and detailed item
descriptions) off-chain in a traditional database, while securely linking it to
an immutable on-chain token via IPFS hashes and Token IDs.<br>
- <b>Theft Prevention &amp; Blacklisting:</b> To provide a mechanism that
allows current owners or administrators to flag items as stolen, mathematically
preventing unauthorized resale or transfer via smart contract restrictions.<br>
- <b>User Experience (UX):</b> To provide a premium, luxury-themed web
interface that abstracts the complexities of Web3 from the end-user while
maintaining high security.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1.4 Feasibility Study<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
- <b>Technical Feasibility:</b> High. The technologies required (Solidity for
smart contracts, PHP for the robust backend API, and Web3.js for <span
class=SpellE>blockchain</span> interaction) are mature, heavily tested, and
well-documented.<br>
- <b>Economic Feasibility:</b> High. By utilizing a local <span class=SpellE>Ethereum</span>
Virtual Machine (EVM) like Hardhat or deploying to a Layer-2 scaling network
(like Polygon), transaction fees (gas) are kept negligible, making the
operational costs highly viable for businesses.<br>
- <b>Operational Feasibility:</b> High. The integration of the <span
class=SpellE>MetaMask</span> browser extension provides a familiar and secure
interface for users to sign transactions. The traditional web interface ensures
that even non-technical users can navigate the platform with ease.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>1.5 Project Scope and Limitations<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
<b>Scope<span class=GramE>:</span></b><br>
- Comprehensive user registration, authentication, and role-based access
control (Admin, Manufacturer/Shop, User).<br>
- Interactive dashboard for minting new <span class=SpellE>jewellery</span>
assets as Non-Fungible Tokens (NFTs) on the <span class=SpellE>Ethereum</span> <span
class=SpellE>blockchain</span>.<br>
- Transferring ownership securely via Solidity smart contracts.<br>
- A public verification portal where anyone can verify an asset's history and
flag items as stolen.<br>
- Reporting modules for administrators to view system usage and asset
distribution.<br>
<br>
<b>Limitations<span class=GramE>:</span></b><br>
- Requires end-users to have a basic understanding of Web3 wallets and have <span
class=SpellE>MetaMask</span> installed.<br>
- Physical asset matching (linking the physical ring to the digital token)
relies on trust in the initial manufacturer or requires physical identifiers
(e.g., microscopic serial numbers, RFID tags, or NFC chips) which are outside
the immediate software scope.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>

<hr size=2 width="100%" align=center>

</span></div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;
mso-border-bottom-alt:solid #CCCCCC .75pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in'>

<h2><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>2. Requirement Specification<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>2.1 System Requirement<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
<b>Software Requirements<span class=GramE>:</span></b><br>
- <b>Operating System:</b> Windows 10/11, Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+), or <span
class=SpellE>macOS</span>.<br>
- <b>Web Browser:</b> Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Microsoft Edge (must
support the <span class=SpellE>MetaMask</span> Extension).<br>
- <b>Local <span class=SpellE>Blockchain</span> Environment:</b> Node.js with
Hardhat or <span class=SpellE>Ganache</span>.<br>
- <b>Server:</b> Apache or <span class=SpellE>Nginx</span> web server (e.g.,
XAMPP/WAMP for local PHP hosting).<br>
<br>
<b>Hardware Specifications (Minimum Requirements):</b><br>
- <b>Processor:</b> Dual-core CPU (Intel Core i3 or AMD equivalent).<br>
- <b>RAM:</b> 4 GB minimum (8 GB strongly recommended for running the local <span
class=SpellE>blockchain</span> node concurrently with the server).<br>
- <b>Storage:</b> 2 GB of free SSD space for application files, local database,
and <span class=SpellE>blockchain</span> state.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>2.2 Technical Requirement<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
- <b>Smart Contract Language:</b> Solidity (v0.8.0 or higher).<br>
- <b>Backend Programming Language:</b> PHP 8.0+ (using PDO for database
interactions).<br>
- <b>Frontend Technologies:</b> HTML5, CSS3 (Custom <span class=SpellE>Glassmorphism</span>
UI), Vanilla JavaScript.<br>
- <span class=SpellE><b>Blockchain</b></span><b> Interface:</b> Web3.js (for
RPC communication between browser and <span class=SpellE>blockchain</span>).<br>
- <b>Database:</b> MySQL 8.0+ or a flat JSON architecture for isolated
environments.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>2.3 Functional Requirements<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
1. <b>User Management:</b> The system shall allow users to register and log in
based on predefined roles (Admin, Shop, <span class=GramE>User</span>).<br>
2. <b>Asset Minting:</b> Authorized shops/manufacturers shall be able to create
a new digital certificate (NFT) for a piece of <span class=SpellE>jewellery</span>.<br>
3. <b>Asset Verification:</b> The system shall provide a search portal where
anyone with a Token ID can verify the asset's authenticity and trace its
current owner.<br>
4. <b>Ownership Transfer:</b> The current owner shall be able to securely
transfer the asset to another registered user using cryptographic signatures.<br>
5. <b>Status Management:</b> Users shall be able to update the status of their
asset (e.g., mark as stolen) to freeze transfers.<br>
6. <b>Admin Reporting:</b> Administrators shall be able to view total assets
minted, user statistics, and system logs.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>2.4 Data &amp; Non-Functional Requirements<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
- <b>Performance Requirement:</b> The off-chain PHP backend must respond to API
queries in under 500ms. On-chain transactions are subject to network block
times.<br>
- <b>Security Requirement:</b> <br>
- All passwords must be hashed using <span class=SpellE>bcrypt</span> (via
PHP's `<span class=SpellE>password_hash</span>`).<br>
- API endpoints must be secured against SQL Injection (using prepared
statements/PDO) and Cross-Site Scripting (XSS).<br>
- Smart contracts must implement strictly tested access controls (e.g., `<span
class=GramE>require(</span><span class=SpellE>msg.sender</span> == owner)`).<br>
- <b>Availability:</b> The web server must maintain 99.9% uptime.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>

<hr size=2 width="100%" align=center>

</span></div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<div style='mso-element:para-border-div;border:none;border-bottom:solid #CCCCCC 1.0pt;
mso-border-bottom-alt:solid #CCCCCC .75pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in'>

<h2><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>3. Database Design<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

</div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>3.1 Identify End Users of the System<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
1. <b>Manufacturer / Shop:</b> The genesis point of the asset. Creates/mints
new <span class=SpellE>jewellery</span>, uploads metadata, and initiates the
first transfer to a customer.<br>
2. <b>Customer / User:</b> The end consumer. Receives ownership of <span
class=SpellE>jewellery</span>, verifies authenticity, and retains the ability
to transfer it to other users in secondary markets.<br>
3. <b>Admin:</b> System overseer. Monitors platform integrity, views aggregate
reports, and manages user suspensions if necessary.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>3.2 ER Diagram (Entities and Attributes)<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
