<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></h3>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>3.3 Tables, Fields, and Relationships<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><br>
- <b>Table: `users`</b><br>
- Stores all authentication and role data. Linked to `<span class=SpellE>jewellery</span>`
via `<span class=SpellE>manufacturer_id</span>` and `<span class=SpellE>current_owner_id</span>`.<br>
- <b>Table: `<span class=SpellE>jewellery</span>`</b><br>
- Stores all off-chain metadata. Reduces the cost of storing heavy strings on
the <span class=SpellE>blockchain</span>. The `<span class=SpellE>token_id</span>`
is the primary bridge to the <span class=SpellE>Ethereum</span> network.<br>
- <b>Table: `<span class=SpellE>transaction_log</span>`</b> <i>(Optional/Future
Expansion)</i><br>
- Keeps a localized, easily <span class=SpellE>queryable</span> cache of
historical ownership transfers to speed up UI rendering without needing to
query the <span class=SpellE>blockchain</span> node for historical events.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<div class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman"'>

<hr size=2 width="100%" align=center>

</span></div>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:"Calibri","sans-serif";mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

